"id":"cmq9gixkw000mqo01ne0lprhh","message":"Thanks for that. And how did you handle state management in those components?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:11:43.616Z","sessionId":"cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt","orderIndex":19},{"id":"cmq9gixkw000nqo016v823v6p","message":"Hmm, I don''t know.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:11:43.616Z","sessionId":"cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt","orderIndex":20},{"id":"cmq9gixkw000oqo01r0mk931d","message":"That’s fine. Let’s move forward. How do you approach collaboration with developers when handing off your designs?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:11:43.616Z","sessionId":"cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt","orderIndex":21},{"id":"cmq9gixkw000pqo01285drpae","message":"I discuss with them and then we create tickets for it and then decide timelines and then go ahead.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:11:43.616Z","sessionId":"cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt","orderIndex":22},{"id":"cmq9gixkw000qqo0133iod0cv","message":"Thank you. One final question: what’s the most challenging design problem you’ve solved recently?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:11:43.616Z","sessionId":"cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt","orderIndex":23},{"id":"cmq9gixkw000rqo01pb5pcoau","message":"Yeah.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:11:43.616Z","sessionId":"cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt","orderIndex":25},{"id":"cmq9gixkw000sqo01vletl4z7","message":"So recently one of the most challenging problems was the payment gateway that I had to resolve and it was getting difficult for me to Make a user make the user experience seamless, but we finally sorted by making provisions in the By using react elements and going developing users stories that can be best","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:11:43.616Z","sessionId":"cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt","orderIndex":26},{"id":"cmq9gixkw000tqo01bd8k388w","message":"Understood. Thank you for your time today, Sam. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:11:43.616Z","sessionId":"cmq9gb46t0003qo01zzg9dlnt","orderIndex":27}],"domain":"product designer","keySkills":["UI Design","React"],"scoringModel":"gpt-4.1-mini","positionTitle":"product designer","mandatoryQuestions":["tell me your self"]}', null, null, 0, null, null, '2026-06-11 12:11:45.62', '2026-06-11 12:11:45.62'), ('cmq9gypfw001pqo01ns724fh1', 'cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p', 'PENDING', null, '{"topic":"Junior role AWS solution architect","turns":[{"id":"cmq9gyns80015qo01itrwlug3","message":"Hello XOXO, I’m Sana from test. Let’s dive right in. Can you tell me about a time when you faced a major challenge at work and how you handled it?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":0},{"id":"cmq9gyns80016qo01hlqrz5m0","message":"um","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":2},{"id":"cmq9gyns80017qo01v15kibe2","message":"Got it, thanks for sharing that. Let’s move on. Can you tell us about your background and how it maps to this AWS Solution Architect role?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":3},{"id":"cmq9gyns80018qo01d27yzi8q","message":"During our deployment, I encountered multiple challenges. One issue was SSH connection failure due to incorrect key permission. I resolved it by assigning a proper permission and verifying the key pair. Another issue occurred when the website was inaccessible. After investigating, I found that port 80 was not allowed in the security group. While working with S3 static website hosting, I faced a deadline error because block public access was enabled and bucket policies were missing. After updating the bucket policy and enabling public access, the issue was resolved. I also encountered CloudFront cache and delays where updated files were not immediately visible. I solved this by creating cache and invalidation and clearing old content. This challenge improved my problem-sorting and problem-solving skill. Thank you.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":4},{"id":"cmq9gyns80019qo0159em67xn","message":"I have completed my BTech in Computer Science and currently I am building my career in Cloud and DevOps. During my learning journey, I have worked on multiple AWS projects where I gained hands-on experience with services like EC2, S3, IAM, VPC and more. One of my projects was hosting a static website on Amazon EC2 using NGX web service. I launched an EC2 instance inside of VPC, configured a security group, installed NGX and deployed the website. I also worked on problem-solving issues related to SSH connectivity, security group and web server configuration, as I am saying. Another project was hosting a static website using S3 and CloudFront. I configured bucket policies, enabled static website hosting and used CloudFront CDN to improve performance and reduce latency. Apart from deployment, I have spent time understanding networking concepts like VPC, subnet, root tables, internet getaway, NAT, getaway and security mechanism. I enjoy troubleshooting infrastructure issues and continuously learning new cloud technology. My goal is to become a skilled cloud and DevOps engineer and contribute to scalable and secure infrastructure solution.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":5},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001aqo01orwqkoie","message":"Thank you for that—sounds like you''ve gained good hands-on experience. Let’s move to the next question. How do you typically approach designing a secure VPC architecture for a new application?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":6},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001bqo01o57upuoe","message":"Amazon VPC stands for Virtual Private Cloud. It is a logical, isolated network in AWS where resources are launched securely. The first step is creating a VPC by defining a CIDR block such as 10.0.0.0.0.16 inside the VPC. Multiple subnets can be created. Public subnets are used to resource that need internet access, while private subnets are used to databases and internal services.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":8},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001cqo01pgghm65q","message":"Thanks for explaining that. Now, how do you approach configuring IAM roles and policies for secure access management?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":9},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001dqo01ryu0wr69","message":"An internet gateway, it attaches to the VPC to provide internet connectivity to public subnets. Root tables control traffic flow between the subnet and external network. Private subnets generally use a NAT gateway to access the internet without exposing resources publicly. Security could provide instance-level security and act as a virtue of firewalls. Network ACLs provide subnet security and are stateless. In one of my projects, I created a custom VPC with public and private subnets, where web servers were deployed in a public subnet while databases were placed in a private subnet. Internet access was provided using the internet, and gateway and outbound access for private. Resource was achieved using a NAT gateway. The architecture helped me to understand secure network design and resource isolation.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":10},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001eqo01qku2c1a8","message":"Mmmmm...","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":11},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001fqo01palbewh0","message":"Take your time. Whenever you''re ready, go ahead and share your thoughts on IAM configuration.","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":12},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001gqo013ooh1r9s","message":"IAM role is one of the most important security features in AWS. IAM stands for Identify and Access Management and IAM role is basically a set of permissions that can be temporarily assumed by AWS service using application to access AWS security. Unlike IAM user, IAM role do not have a permanent credit such as username, password or access key. Instead of AWS security token service, SDS provides temporary credit rate and whenever a service or a user assumes this role, for example, if an EC2 instance needs to access an S3 bucket, it should not store access key inside the server because that creates a security risk. Instead, we create an IAM role with the security S3 permission and attach that role to the EC2 instance whenever the application running inside EC2 instance access to S3. AWS automatically provides a temporary credit through the role. This follows the principle of least privilege, which means granting only the minimum permission required to perform a task.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":13},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001hqo01m6wjgthv","message":"Thank you, that’s a solid overview. For our final question, how do you ensure high availability when designing with EC2?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":14},{"id":"cmq9gyns8001iqo01g5mnd644","message":"The object of this EC2 is to understand how the web applications are hosted on the cloud server and how the networking components work together. First of all, I have to create a VPC environment and configure a network component. Then I launch an EC2 instance running Amazon Linux. While creating the instance, I generated a key pair for a secure SSH access and configured security group to allow inbound traffic on port 22 for SSH and port 80 for HTTP access. After launching the instance, I connected to the server using SSH. Once connected, I updated the server package and installed Nivex web server.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":16},{"id":"cmq9gyns9001jqo016suflgeg","message":"After successfully installation, I start enable a service so that it would automatically start after system reboot. Then uploaded a website file including HTML, CSS, JavaScript into the web server directly. Once the deployment was completed, I test the website using the public IP address of the EC2 instance and verified that it was accessible for the internet. During the implement I faced when the website was not loading after investigation, I found that the HTTP port was not properly configured in the security group. After opening a port number to the website, the website became accessible.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":17},{"id":"cmq9gyns9001kqo012iy0zo5l","message":"Understood. Let’s wrap up. Thank you for your time today. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":18},{"id":"cmq9gyns9001lqo01o9jta0ro","message":"That''s all.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:23:57.416Z","sessionId":"cmq9gjjw30011qo0109dn7g5p","orderIndex":19}],"domain":"AWS Solution architect","keySkills":["EC2","S3","VPC","IAN"],"scoringModel":"gpt-4.1-mini","positionTitle":"AWS Solution architect","mandatoryQuestions":["Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role."]}', null, null, 0, null, null, '2026-06-11 12:23:59.564', '2026-06-11 12:23:59.564'), ('cmq9hej6q0021qo01tiwro1b0', 'cmq9hdpw0001vqo01c5q6upb0', 'PENDING', null, '{"topic":"senior devloper","turns":[{"id":"cmq9hehok001xqo01tac1tgt3","message":"Hi, this is Sana from test. Welcome to the interview. Let''s jump right in. Can you tell me about a challenging problem you solved recently and how you approached it?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-11T12:36:16.005Z","sessionId":"cmq9hdpw0001vqo01c5q6upb0","orderIndex":0}],"domain":"product designer","keySkills":["UI Design","React"],"scoringModel":"gpt-4.1-mini","positionTitle":"product designer","mandatoryQuestions":["tell me your self"]}', null, null, 0, null, null, '2026-06-11 12:36:17.955', '2026-06-11 12:36:17.955'), ('cmqam2808000grq01riyuuink', 'cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6', 'PENDING', null, '{"topic":"hr","turns":[{"id":"cmqam26gp0006rq014w3r1qd5","message":"Hello, drashtitest. I''m Sana from test. Let''s begin. Can you tell me about a time when you overcame a significant challenge in a professional setting?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T07:34:25.850Z","sessionId":"cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6","orderIndex":0,"timestampMs":304},{"id":"cmqam26gp0007rq01jwlurylr","message":"I first identified the root cause of the issue, gathered relevant information, advocated possible solutions, and then implemented the most effective approach. I also communicated regularly with the stakeholders and monitored the results to ensure the problem","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T07:34:25.850Z","sessionId":"cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6","orderIndex":1,"timestampMs":11429},{"id":"cmqam26gp0008rq01pges940a","message":"Thank you. Can you share a bit more about what specific HR challenge you faced in that situation?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T07:34:25.850Z","sessionId":"cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6","orderIndex":2,"timestampMs":50224},{"id":"cmqam26gp0009rq015jwgwba1","message":"My most difficult task was handling urgent hiring for multiple positions, similarly violating the strict deadlines. I managed candidates to succeed, screening interview coordinators and follow-ups efficiently. For proper planning and communication, I successfully closed the position on time. you","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T07:34:25.850Z","sessionId":"cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6","orderIndex":3,"timestampMs":62910},{"id":"cmqam26gp000arq01fmuugwyu","message":"Understood. Now, tell me about your background and how it maps to this HR role.","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T07:34:25.850Z","sessionId":"cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6","orderIndex":4,"timestampMs":97881},{"id":"cmqam26gp000brq01eurek44y","message":"I am a fresher in HR, but I have a strong interest in human resource and talent acquisition. Throughout my academic background and project, I learned about the recruitment process, employee onboarding, performance management, HR policies. I have good communication, interpersonal skill, and I work to apply my knowledge in professional HR environment while continuing to learn and improve.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T07:34:25.850Z","sessionId":"cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6","orderIndex":5,"timestampMs":107687},{"id":"cmqam26gp000crq01jr2mq8sg","message":"Thank you for sharing that. How have you applied your problem-solving skills in an HR context?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T07:34:25.850Z","sessionId":"cmqaly6tw0004rq0135rrnjz6","orderIndex":6,"timestampMs":140486}],"domain":"hr","keySkills":["hr Fundamentals","Problem Solving & Judgment","Domain Expertise","Communication","Professional Standards"],"scoringModel":"gpt-4.1-mini","positionTitle":"hr","mandatoryQuestions":["Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role."]}', null, null, 0, null, null, '2026-06-12 07:34:27.848', '2026-06-12 07:34:27.848'), ('cmqanfu2j0018rq012tdkg4o5', 'cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5', 'PENDING', null, '{"topic":"Graduate trainee","turns":[{"id":"cmqanfscq000qrq01w0nhzgsj","message":"Hi Raju, this is Sana from Test. Let''s begin. Can you tell me about a challenging project you worked on recently and what your role was?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":0,"timestampMs":1},{"id":"cmqanfscq000rrq015fp27vq6","message":"Hello.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":1,"timestampMs":2541},{"id":"cmqanfscq000srq01s4m5jx2o","message":"Hello Raju, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s begin. Could you briefly explain what the first law of thermodynamics is?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":2,"timestampMs":18490},{"id":"cmqanfscq000trq0155386ew4","message":"The first law of thermodynamics tells you about conservation of energy, it says that energy cannot be created nor destroyed, it can just change its form from one to the other.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":3,"timestampMs":29257},{"id":"cmqanfscq000urq012n1ziuc3","message":"Thank you, that’s correct. Now, can you describe a common manufacturing process used in mechanical engineering?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":4,"timestampMs":59723},{"id":"cmqanfscq000vrq019fbykeg3","message":"Yes casting is one of the common manufacturing processes which is used","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":5,"timestampMs":68130},{"id":"cmqanfscq000wrq01vnwgf9d9","message":"Understood. Could you give a brief outline of how the casting process works?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":6,"timestampMs":91478},{"id":"cmqanfscq000xrq01cjdbb2d6","message":"So, in casting molten metal is poured into the dye, it is allowed to cool and then the product is taken out, there are some finishing processes done and you get the final product. Thank you.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":7,"timestampMs":97691},{"id":"cmqanfscq000yrq010h1i2t3a","message":"Thank you for that. Let''s move on. Could you explain what additive manufacturing is and how it differs from traditional methods?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":8,"timestampMs":130178},{"id":"cmqanfscq000zrq01k852ekca","message":"Additive manufacturing is basically a process in which a product is manufactured by depositing layers of the base metal and is done layer by layer.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":9,"timestampMs":138972},{"id":"cmqanfscq0010rq019atr8ayd","message":"Thank you. And how does that differ from something like subtractive manufacturing?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":10,"timestampMs":171143},{"id":"cmqanfscq0011rq014cgcz4ak","message":"Subtractive Manufacturing is the most traditional method and Subtractive Manufacturing is faster to manufacture as well as by the editing manufacturing it takes much more time to finish the final product.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":11,"timestampMs":181094},{"id":"cmqanfscq0012rq01nv3psoal","message":"Got it. One last question for today—how would you decide when to use additive versus subtractive manufacturing?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":12,"timestampMs":211679},{"id":"cmqanfscq0013rq01u36ok0e6","message":"If the product is very complex to manufacture and it involves multiple processes or probably it is difficult to manufacture from the traditional processes, I will go for additive manufacturing. If the manufacturing process needs speed and products are simple to make, then I will decide to go for active manufacturing. Thank you.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":13,"timestampMs":220772},{"id":"cmqanfscq0014rq01ct886w41","message":"Thank you for your explanation. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:13:00.362Z","sessionId":"cmqan99y1000mrq01b6rrq8b5","orderIndex":14,"timestampMs":257319}],"domain":"Junior mechanical engineer","keySkills":["Thermodynamics","Manufacturing"],"scoringModel":"gpt-4.1-mini","positionTitle":"Junior mechanical engineer","mandatoryQuestions":["Laws of thermodyanmics","manufacturing process","additive manufacturing"]}', null, null, 0, null, null, '2026-06-12 08:13:02.585', '2026-06-12 08:13:02.585'), ('cmqanrjq5001yrq013v5jpofc', 'cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd', 'PENDING', null, '{"topic":"senior devloper","turns":[{"id":"cmqanri97001erq01orcwxbmc","message":"Hi Raju, this is Sana from Test. Let’s dive into the interview. Can you tell me about a challenging project you recently worked on and how you handled it?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":0,"timestampMs":0},{"id":"cmqanri97001frq019aorqagg","message":"Hello.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":1,"timestampMs":0},{"id":"cmqanri97001grq019oeqd3ip","message":"Hi Raju, my name is Sana, and I’ll be conducting your interview today. Let’s dive right in. To start off, tell me about yourself.","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":2,"timestampMs":12763},{"id":"cmqanri97001hrq01aqcf1qk3","message":"I am Raju from Mumbai. I have five years of experience in product design and development. I work for companies like Google and Apple. I have worked in building e-commerce platforms, prototyping as well as certain products where I used to make the MVP and 3D model and then convert it into the final product.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":3,"timestampMs":23486},{"id":"cmqanri97001irq0198x3vja3","message":"Thank you for that introduction. Can you tell me more about your experience with UI design in those projects?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":4,"timestampMs":73975},{"id":"cmqanri97001jrq01nyrb8yeb","message":"Yes, so UI design for me was limited to wireframing and conceptual withstanding where I was more into converting the ideas into designs or drawings in the paper followed by building mock-ups on Figma.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":5,"timestampMs":82744},{"id":"cmqanri97001krq011rd87uka","message":"Got it. How comfortable are you with using React in your product development work?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":6,"timestampMs":120668},{"id":"cmqanri97001lrq019a9unwby","message":"I can say on a scale of five, I am good with React Act 2 or 3. I have used React for making components and reusable toolkits from the library for certain assignments in my previous projects. I have used React for making components and reusable toolkits from the library for certain assignments in my previous projects. I have used React for making components and reusable toolkits from the library for certain","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":7,"timestampMs":128684},{"id":"cmqanri97001mrq01qxmsqhfu","message":"Understood. Can you give an example of a project where you used React components in your product design work?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":8,"timestampMs":164625},{"id":"cmqanri97001nrq01u35hiwd8","message":"Yeah, so I used it for browser building as well as ready-made react component for the payment gateway","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":9,"timestampMs":174404},{"id":"cmqanri97001orq01c1erkg7y","message":"Thanks for sharing that. Could you tell me about a specific challenge you faced when integrating those components?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":10,"timestampMs":196730},{"id":"cmqanri97001prq01ng5ny897","message":"Yeah, so the user interface was not really intuitive, so we used to get a lot of dropouts during the payment because it was not as user-friendly as it should be. So that was one of the problems. How did I tackle it is basically developing user stories and looking to the perspectives of how a user might interact and where exactly does it decide to not go through the payment.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":11,"timestampMs":210461},{"id":"cmqanri97001qrq012x00ksop","message":"Makes sense. And what was one key improvement you made to address that issue?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":12,"timestampMs":260596},{"id":"cmqanri97001rrq0199mki41d","message":"Key improvement was we kept it as simple as possible so to make a purchase the customer does not really need to log in or create an account on the platform, they can directly you know enter their basic information and make a payment and they get the details of their order directly on the given what is given ID email ID or mobile number making it much more seamless and easier for them to place an order","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":13,"timestampMs":270764},{"id":"cmqanri97001srq01aav7zxh6","message":"Thank you, that’s a solid approach. One final question: how do you stay updated on the latest trends in product design?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":14,"timestampMs":323694},{"id":"cmqanri97001trq01yfii2gbq","message":"I follow certain pages on LinkedIn and a few channels specifically on products on YouTube. Other than that, I keep reading articles in newspaper and product magazines and so on.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":15,"timestampMs":336960},{"id":"cmqanri97001urq013qxbhvta","message":"Great, that’s helpful to know. Thank you for your time today. This concludes our interview. Best of luck with the hiring process.","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T08:22:07.147Z","sessionId":"cmqangixr001crq01f09ldzyd","orderIndex":16,"timestampMs":375188}],"domain":"product designer","keySkills":["UI Design","React"],"scoringModel":"gpt-4.1-mini","positionTitle":"product designer","mandatoryQuestions":["tell me your self"]}', null, null, 0, null, null, '2026-06-12 08:22:09.053', '2026-06-12 08:22:09.053'), ('cmqaqoymm000nmv018utkvigp', 'cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29', 'PENDING', null, '{"topic":"Junior role AWS solution architect","turns":[{"id":"cmqaqowli0008mv01m0syn835","message":"Hello Thor, this is Sana from test. Welcome! Let’s get started right away. Can you tell me about a project where you faced a major challenge and how you overcame it?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":0,"timestampMs":435},{"id":"cmqaqowli0009mv01p84m7bqv","message":"Yeah, basically, I used two projects like first one is a static website hosting on EC2. Actually, one of the project I worked on was deploying a static website on Amazon EC2. I launched a Ubuntu instance, configured a security group instance, like installed Naginx and hosted the application. I also configured SSH access using TPS and managed firewalls rule through the security group. The challenges I faced like website was not inaccessible from browser, port 80 was not allowed in security group and when I solved this, like I modified inbound rule and allowed HTTP traffic on port 80 from anywhere. This is the first one. The second one is resume using S3 and CloudFront. Actually, in this website on Amazon S3 using a static website hosting and integrated CloudFront for global content, delivery and low latency. I configured a bucket policy to allow read access and enable caching through CloudFront. The challenge is access delay and error. Bucket policy was incorrect. Then I resolved with update the bucket policy and configured a public read permission.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":1,"timestampMs":12255},{"id":"cmqaqowli000amv01lr4kobe3","message":"Thanks for sharing. Now, tell us a bit about your background and how it maps to this AWS Solution Architect role.","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":2,"timestampMs":108745},{"id":"cmqaqowli000bmv01gxdyk584","message":"Actually I have completed my B.Tech in Computer Science Engineering and currently I am focusing on Cloud and AWS technology. During my learning and hands-on practice, I work instinctively with the core AWS services such as EC2, S3, IAM and VPC. I have built multiple projects involving website hosting, secure network architecture, access management and cloud infrastructure. I am interested in designing a scalable and secure architecture. Apart from AWS services, I also have knowledge of Linux administration, networking fundamentals, Git and basic DevOps concepts. While working on the project, I learned how to important security, availability and cost optimization are in cloud environments. I enjoy troubleshooting issues, understanding root cause and implementing reliable solutions. My goal is to become a solution architect who can design a highly affordable, scalable and secure infrastructure according to my business requirements.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":3,"timestampMs":118427},{"id":"cmqaqowli000cmv01aenu58gq","message":"Understood. Let’s dive a bit deeper. Can you walk me through how you''ve used IAM roles in your projects?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":4,"timestampMs":192935},{"id":"cmqaqowli000dmv01jcsipw38","message":"Identify and access management, commonly referred to IAM, is the service responsible for authentication and authorization in AWS. IAM enables the administration to securely manage user group, role and permission through IAM organization, and control who can access AWS resources and what actions they are not allowed to perform. IAM users represent individual identities, group collections of users with similar permissions. Policies are JSON documents that define permissions. Roles provide temporary credit intel and are generally assigned to AWS services rather than individuals. One of the most important principles followed in IAM is the principle of least privilege. According to this principle, users and services should only be granted the minimum permission necessary to perform their task. Multi-factor authentication adds on an additional layer of security by requiring a secondary authentication mechanism. IAM roles are widely used to provide secure access between AWS services without exposing access keys. For example, an EC2 instance can access an S3 bucket through an IAM role instead of storing credit details inside the application. At last, IAM is fundamental to AWS security because it ensures proper access control, minimizes security risks, and simplifies permission management. That''s all. Thank you.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":5,"timestampMs":203293},{"id":"cmqaqowli000emv015gq8cc9r","message":"Thank you. How have you applied the principle of least privilege in a specific project scenario?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":6,"timestampMs":323858},{"id":"cmqaqowli000fmv01c3j7luxu","message":"I would put the application behind the application load balancer and configure autoscaling multiple EC2 instances across different availability zones to distribute traffic. Statics content would be moved to S3 and server through a CloudFront to reduce the load on web servers. Monitoring would be configured using a CloudWatch and alarms. The architecture improves performance, scalability, and availability.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":7,"timestampMs":334813},{"id":"cmqaqowli000gmv010j6o0wf6","message":"Understood. Let me ask a follow-up: how did you ensure that only necessary permissions were granted to those EC2 instances?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":8,"timestampMs":379188},{"id":"cmqaqowli000hmv01v3m3s8hk","message":"Thank you.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":10,"timestampMs":459070},{"id":"cmqaqowli000imv01txginf5w","message":"😲😲😲😲😲😲😲","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":12,"timestampMs":474841},{"id":"cmqaqowli000jmv0123uhe0r7","message":"Thanks for that. Let’s move to the next area. How have you designed a VPC for a secure and scalable solution?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:44:04.614Z","sessionId":"cmqajccxy000bmt016f2r4r29","orderIndex":13,"timestampMs":487247}],"domain":"AWS Solution architect","keySkills":["EC2","S3","VPC","IAN"],"scoringModel":"gpt-4.1-mini","positionTitle":"AWS Solution architect","mandatoryQuestions":["Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role."]}', null, null, 0, null, null, '2026-06-12 09:44:07.245', '2026-06-12 09:44:07.245'), ('cmqaqrs6g000ymv01qdvjw1ib', 'cmqaqqgd9000tmv01g12fkzuc', 'PENDING', null, '{"topic":"Junior role AWS solution architect","turns":[],"domain":"AWS Solution architect","keySkills":["EC2","S3","VPC","IAN"],"scoringModel":"gpt-4.1-mini","positionTitle":"AWS Solution architect","mandatoryQuestions":["Tell us about your background and how it maps to this role."]}', null, null, 0, null, null, '2026-06-12 09:46:18.856', '2026-06-12 09:46:18.856'), ('cmqar6fy8001qmv01e3r93nnw', 'cmqaqskju0010mv01zlahv6lh', 'PENDING', null, '{"topic":"Junior role AWS solution architect","turns":[{"id":"cmqar6ej10012mv01ky6un6aa","message":"Hi Gargee, this is Sana from Test. Let''s begin. Can you tell me about a time when you had to solve a difficult problem under pressure?","speaker":"INTERVIEWER","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:57:41.005Z","sessionId":"cmqaqskju0010mv01zlahv6lh","orderIndex":0,"timestampMs":543},{"id":"cmqar6ej10013mv01zd34l7rl","message":"Once the project I worked was on deployment or static website on Amazon EC2, I launched an Ubuntu instance, configure, config security group, install NIC key and hosted the application. I also config SSH access using key pairs and manage firewall through security groups. Thank you.","speaker":"CANDIDATE","createdAt":"2026-06-12T09:57: